          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            = succeed "," do
              %strong lax-idempotent 2-monad
            %strong Kock–Zöberlein
            or
            = succeed "," do
              %strong KZ 2-monad
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stuff%2C+structure%2C+property"} property-like structure
            that a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
          %p
            Lax-idempotent 2-monads have occasionally also been called
            %strong KZ monads
            in the literature, but this terminology may be confusing, as it is inconsistent with terminology of
            = succeed ":" do
              %strong
                lax-idempotent
                = succeed "-monads" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally-discrete+2-category"} locally-discrete 2-category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+monad"} idempotence
          %p
            The archetypal examples are given by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-monads"} 2-monads
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            that take a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+cocompletion"} free cocompletion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T C
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            under a given class of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
            – then an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudoalgebra+for+a+2-monad"} algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T C \to C
            is a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            with all such colimits, which are of course essentially unique. Moreover, given thus-cocomplete categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \colon C \to D
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi colim
                  %mi T
                  %mi F
                  %mi S
                  %mo →
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi colim
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} colim T F S \to F(colim S)
            given by the universal property of the colimit. It is this property that lax-idempotence generalizes.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-monad"} 2-monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            is called
            %strong lax-idempotent
            if given any two (strict)
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi T
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \colon T A \to A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi T
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \colon T B \to B
            and a morphism
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon A \to B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi b
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi T
                  %mi f
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mi f
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar f \colon b \circ T f \Rightarrow f \circ a
            making
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %mover
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f,\bar f)
            a lax morphism of
            = succeed "-algebras:" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi T
                          %mi A
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %mi T
                              %mi f
                        %mtd
                          %mi T
                          %mi B
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⇙
                          %mover
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mi b
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo →
                            %mi f
                        %mtd
                          %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  T A &amp; \overset{T f}{\to} &amp; T B \\
                  a \downarrow &amp; \swArrow \bar f &amp; \downarrow b \\
                  A &amp; \underset{f}{\to} &amp; B
                  }
          %p
            Dually, a 2-monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            is called
            %strong colax-idempotent
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon A \to B
            gives rise to a colax
            = succeed "-morphism" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f,\tilde f)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi T
                          %mi A
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %mi T
                              %mi f
                        %mtd
                          %mi T
                          %mi B
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⇗
                          %mover
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mi b
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo →
                            %mi f
                        %mtd
                          %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  T A &amp; \overset{T f}{\to} &amp; T B \\
                  a \downarrow &amp; \neArrow \tilde f &amp; \downarrow b \\
                  A &amp; \underset{f}{\to} &amp; B
                  }
          %h3#equivalent_conditions Equivalent conditions
          %p
            A 2-monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mo ,
                  %mi μ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi η
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (T, \mu, \eta)
            is lax idempotent if and only if, for every object
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %msub
                    %mi η
                    %mi A
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msub
                    %mi μ
                    %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \eta_A \dashv \mu_A
            with invertible unit or an adjunction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi μ
                    %mi A
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msub
                    %mi η
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu_A \dashv \eta_{T A}
            with invertible counit (with either adjunction implying the other). Notice that it is already enough to have either adjoint since the unit resp. counit will be invertible through the axioms of the 2-monad.
          %p
            An extensive list of equivalent conditions is given on the page of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax-idempotent+2-adjunction"} lax-idempotent 2-adjunction
          #AlgebraAdjoint.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              A 2-monad
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              as above, with unit
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi η
                      %mo :
                      %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta: 1 \to T
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi T
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \colon T A \to A
              there is a 2-cell
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi θ
                      %mi a
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ⇒
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi A
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta_a \colon 1 \Rightarrow \eta_A \circ a
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi θ
                      %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mn 1
                          %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\theta_a ,1_{1_A})
              are the unit and counit of an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ⊣
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \dashv \eta_A
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              %strong> (Adapted from Kelly–Lack)
              \. The multiplication
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi μ
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi T
                      %mn 2
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu_A \colon T^2 A \to T A
              is a
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_A \colon A \to T A
              is a morphism from the underlying object of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              to that of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi μ
                        %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu_A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi η
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi μ
                      %mi A
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi T
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi A
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                        %mi A
                    %mo ⇒
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi A
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar\eta_A \colon \mu_A \circ T \eta_A = 1_{T A} \Rightarrow \eta_A \circ a
              making
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_A
              into a lax
              = succeed "-morphism." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi θ
                        %mi a
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mi η
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                        %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta_a = \bar\eta_A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} triangle equalities
              then require that:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %msub
                          %mover
                            %mi η
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                          %mi A
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi a
                        %mo ⇒
                        %mi a
                        %mo ∘
                        %msub
                          %mi η
                          %mi A
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi a
                        %mo =
                        %mi a
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \bar\eta_A \colon a \Rightarrow a \circ \eta_A \circ a = a
                  is equal to
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mn 1
                            %mi a
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_a
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ∘
                        %msub
                          %mover
                            %mi η
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                          %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \circ \bar\eta_A
                  makes
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ∘
                        %msub
                          %mi η
                          %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \circ \eta_A
                  a lax
                  = succeed "-morphism" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi T
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
                  to
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
                  (paste
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mover
                            %mi η
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                          %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar\eta_A
                  with the identity square
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi a
                          %mo ∘
                          %msub
                            %mi μ
                            %mi A
                          %mo =
                          %mi a
                          %mo ∘
                          %mi T
                          %mi a
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \circ \mu_A = a \circ T a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi a
                          %mo ∘
                          %msub
                            %mi η
                            %mi A
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mn 1
                            %mi A
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \circ \eta_A = 1_A
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mn 1
                          %mi a
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_a
                  also makes this into a lax
                  = succeed "-morphism," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi T
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi a
                          %msub
                            %mover
                              %mi η
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                            %mi A
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mn 1
                            %mi a
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \bar\eta_A = 1_a
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mover
                            %mi η
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                          %mi A
                        %msub
                          %mi η
                          %mi A
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %msub
                          %mi η
                          %mi A
                        %mo ⇒
                        %msub
                          %mi η
                          %mi A
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi a
                        %mo ∘
                        %msub
                          %mi η
                          %mi A
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi η
                          %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar\eta_A \eta_A \colon \eta_A \Rightarrow \eta_A \circ a \circ \eta_A = \eta_A
                  is equal to
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mn 1
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi η
                                %mi A
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_{\eta_A}
                  = succeed "-morphism" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi T
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mover
                              %mi η
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                            %mi A
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar\eta_A
            %p
              Conversely, suppose
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi θ
                        %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta_a
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a,b
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A,B
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon A \to B
              are given. Take
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar f
              to be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mate"} mate
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi T
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi η
                    %mi A
                    %mo =
                    %mi f
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_f \colon b \circ T f \circ \eta A = f \Rightarrow f
              with respect to the adjunctions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \dashv \eta_A
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ⊣
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \dashv 1
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi θ
                        %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta_a
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                      %mo =
                      %mi b
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi T
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mi θ
                        %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar f = b \circ T f \circ \theta_a
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar f
              in turn is given by
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                      %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar f \circ \eta_A
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_f
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar f
              satisfies the unit condition.
            %p
              Consider the diagrams expressing the multiplication condition: because
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi μ
                      %mi A
                    %mo =
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi T
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \circ \mu_A = a \circ T a
              (and the same for
              = succeed ")," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                      %mo ,
                      %mi β
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi b
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi T
                      %mi b
                      %mo ∘
                      %msup
                        %mi T
                        %mn 2
                      %mi f
                      %mo ⇒
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi a
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi T
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha, \beta \colon b \circ T b \circ T^2 f \Rightarrow f \circ a \circ T a
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %msub
                      %mi θ
                      %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi T
                    %mi a
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi T
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (T\theta_a, 1) \colon T a \dashv T\eta_A
              are given by pasting with
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \eta_A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar f
              pasted with
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mover
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi T
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mi A
                      %mo =
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi T
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mi f
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mrow
                          %mi T
                          %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \bar f \circ T \eta_A = T(f \circ \eta_A) = T 1_f = 1_{T f}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \eta_A
              with the identity
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi μ
                      %mi B
                    %mo ∘
                    %msup
                      %mi T
                      %mn 2
                    %mi f
                    %mo =
                    %mi T
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi μ
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu_B \circ T^2 f = T f \circ \mu_A
              (and then pasting with
              = succeed ")," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar f
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi μ
                      %mi A
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi T
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi A
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                        %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu_A \circ T \eta_A = 1_{T A}
              this is also equal to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mrow
                          %mi T
                          %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_{T f}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar f
              is indeed a lax
              = succeed "-morphism." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
          %p
            Since
            = succeed "\u2018s" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi μ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
            makes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            itself into a (generalized)
            = succeed "-algebra," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modification"} modification
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℓ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi T
                        %mn 2
                  %mo →
                  %mi η
                  %mi T
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi μ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ell \colon 1_{T^2} \to \eta T \circ \mu
            making
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℓ
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi μ
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi η
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\ell,1) \colon \mu \dashv \eta T
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi T
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \colon T A \to A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi θ
                    %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta_a
            is given by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi ℓ
                      %mi A
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi T
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T a \circ \ell_A \circ T \eta_A
          %p
            A different but equivalent condition is that there be a modification
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi T
                  %mi η
                  %mo →
                  %mi η
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \colon T \eta \to \eta T
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mi η
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \eta = 1
            and
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                    %mi d
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu d = 1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℓ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ell
            as above,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            is given by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℓ
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi T
                    %mi η
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ell \circ T \eta
          %p
            These various conditions can also be regarded as ways to say that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Moore+category"} Eilenberg-Moore adjunction
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax-idempotent+2-adjunction"} lax-idempotent 2-adjunction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            is a lax-idempotent 2-monad exactly when this 2-adjunction is lax-idempotent, and therefore also just when it is the 2-monad induced by
            %em some
            lax-idempotent 2-adjunction.
          %p
            Dually, for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            to be colax-idempotent, it is necessary and sufficient that any of the following hold.
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                For any
                = succeed "-algebra" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi T
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \colon T A \to A
                there is a 2-cell
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ζ
                        %mi a
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mi A
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi a
                      %mo ⇒
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \zeta_a \colon \eta_A \circ a \Rightarrow 1
                such that
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi ζ
                          %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %msub
                          %mi η
                          %mi A
                        %mo ⊣
                        %mi a
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1,\zeta_a) \colon \eta_A \dashv a
            %li
              %p
                There is a modification
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi μ
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi η
                      %mi T
                      %mo →
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m \colon \mu \circ \eta T \to 1
                making
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi m
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi η
                        %mi T
                        %mo ⊣
                        %mi μ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1,m) \colon \eta T \dashv \mu
            %li
              %p
                There is a modification
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi η
                      %mi T
                      %mo →
                      %mi T
                      %mi η
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \colon \eta T \to T\eta
                such that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                      %mi η
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e\eta = 1
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi μ
                        %mi e
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu e = 1
          %h2#algebras Algebras
          %p
            Theorem
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AlgebraAdjoint"}
            gives a necessary condition for an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            to admit a
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi η
                    %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi T
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_A : A \to T A
            admit a left adjoint with identity counit. In the case of pseudo algebras, this necessary condition is also sufficient.
          #PseudoAlgebras.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              To give a pseudo
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is equivalently to give a left adjoint to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi A
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_A : A\to T A
              with invertible counit.
          %p
            In particular, an object admits at most one pseudo
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/property-like+structure"} property-like structure
          %p
            In many cases it is interesting to consider the pseudo
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T A \to A
            has a further left adjoint, forming an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triple"} adjoint triple
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+algebras"} continuous algebras
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
            As mentioned above, the standard examples of lax-idempotent 2-monads are those on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            whose algebras are categories with all colimits of a specified class. In this case, the 2-monad is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+cocompletion"} free cocompletion
            operation. Dually, there are colax-idempotent 2-monads which adjoin limits of a specified class. A converse is given by (
            %a{:href => "#PowerCattaniWinskel"}> PowerCattaniWinskel
            ), who show that a 2-monad is a monad for free cocompletions if and only if it is lax-idempotent and the unit
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi η
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
            is dense (plus a coherence condition).
          %p
            Another important example of a colax-idempotent 2-monad is the monad on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat/B
            that takes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \colon E \to B
            to the projection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi p
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B/p \to B
            out of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+category"} comma category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+fibrations"} Grothendieck fibrations
            over
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration+in+a+2-category"} fibration in a 2-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \mapsto p/B
            is lax-idempotent, and its algebras are opfibrations.
          %p
            This latter is actually a special case of a general situation. If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            is a (2-)monad relative to which one can define
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+multicategories"} generalized multicategories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde{T}
            on the 2-category of such generalized multicategories (aka “virtual
            = succeed "-algebras\u201D)," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde{T}
            = succeed "-algebras." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            is the 2-monad whose algebras are strict 2-functors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B\to Cat
            and whose pseudo algebras are pseudofunctors
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B\to Cat
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde{T}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multicategories"} multicategories
            whose pseudo algebras are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+categories"} monoidal categories
          %h2#properties Properties
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-distributive+laws"} pseudo-distributive laws
                involving lax-idempotent 2-monads have an especially nice form; see
                %a{:href => "#MarmolejoDL"} (Marmolejo)
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "#WalkerDL"} (Walker)
            %li
              %p
                For ordinary 1-monads there exists a presentation due to Manes as “Kleisli triples” with primary data a family of unit morphisms and lifts avoiding the iteration of the endofunctor. A similar presentation exists for lax-idempotent 2-monads as shown in Marmolejo-Wood (
                %a{:href => "#MW12"}> 2012
                ). It is shown then in Walker
                %a{:href => "#WalkerYS"} (2017)
                that provided the units of this presentation are fully faithful (a reflection of the fully-faithfulness of the Yoneda embedding) (almost) all the axioms of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+structure"} Yoneda structure
                are satisfied. In cases where size plays no role like e.g. the ideal completion of posets the two concepts coincide. For further details see at
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+structure"} Yoneda structure
                or Walker
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "#WalkerYS"} (2017)
          %h2#laxidempotent_2comonads Lax-idempotent 2-comonads
          %p
            The dualisation of the notion of lax-idempotent 2-monad is a little subtle. By definition, a
            %strong lax-idempotent 2-comonad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            should be one for which every 1-cell between
            = succeed "-coalgebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+morphism"} lax morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi f
                        %mtd
                          %mi D
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo
                            %mi c
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⇙
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mi d
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi W
                          %mi C
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %mi W
                              %mi f
                        %mtd
                          %mi W
                          %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{ C &amp; \overset{f}{\to} &amp; D\\
                  ^{c} \downarrow &amp; \swArrow &amp; \downarrow^{d}\\
                  W C &amp; \underset{W f}{\to} &amp; W D}
          %p The following are then equivalent.
          %ol
            %li
              The 2-comonad
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi W
                    %mo ,
                    %mi δ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ε
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (W, \delta, \varepsilon)
              is lax-idempotent.
            %li
              There is an adjoint triple
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ε
                      %mi W
                      %mo ⊣
                      %mi δ
                      %mo ⊣
                      %mi W
                      %mi ε
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varepsilon W \dashv \delta \dashv W\varepsilon
            %li
              An object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is a
              = succeed "-coalgebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ε
                      %mi A
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi DA
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varepsilon_A : A \to DA
              admits a right adjoint with invertible unit.
          %p Consequently:
          %ul
            %li
              a lax-idempotent 2-monad on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi K
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K^{op}
              is a lax-idempotent 2-comonad on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %li
              a lax-idempotent 2-monad on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi K
                      %mi co
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K^{co}
              is a colax-idempotent 2-monad on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %li
              a lax-idempotent 2-monad on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi K
                      %mi coop
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K^{coop}
              is a colax-idempotent 2-comonad on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
          %p However, be warned that the conventions for what “colax-idempotent 2-comonad” means in the literature are inconsistent.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+monad"} idempotent monad
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-monad"} 2-monad
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stuff%2C+structure%2C+property"} stuff, structure, property
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/property-like+structure"} property-like structure
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+algebra"} continuous algebra
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+cocompletion"} free cocompletion
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax-idempotent+2-adjunction"} lax-idempotent 2-adjunction
          %h2#references References
          %p Classical references are
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Max+Kelly"}> Max Kelly
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steve+Lack"} Steve Lack
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On property-like structures
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/1997/n9/3-09abs.html"} abstract
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anders+Kock"}> Anders Kock
                ,
                %em Monads for which structures are adjoint to units
                , Aarhus Preprint 1972/73 No. 35. (
                %a{:href => "http://home.imf.au.dk/kock/msau1.PDF"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anders+Kock"}> Anders Kock
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Monads for which structures are adjoint to units
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ross+Street"}> Ross Street
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Fibrations and Yoneda’s lemma in a 2-category
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0063102"} doi:10.1007/BFb0063102
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ross+Street"}> Ross Street
                ,
                %em Fibrations in Bicategories
                , Cah. Top. Géom. Diff.
                %strong XXI
                no.2 (1980). (
                %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item?id=CTGDC_1980__21_2_111_0"}> numdam
                )
            %li
              %p
                Volker Zöberlein,
                %em Doctrines on 2-categories
                , Math. Zeitschrift
                %strong 148
                (1976) pp.267-279. (
                %a{:href => "https://gdz.sub.uni-goettingen.de/id/PPN266833020_0148?tify={%22pages%22:[273],%22view%22:%22info%22}"}> gdz
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Francisco+Marmolejo"}> Francisco Marmolejo
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Doctrines whose structure forms a fully faithful adjoint string
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/1997/n2/3-02abs.html"} TAC
          %p Textbook accounts:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"}> Peter Johnstone
                ,
                %em Sketches of an elephant vol.1
                , Oxford UP 2004. (B1.1.11, pp.250-54)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marta+Bunge"}> Marta Bunge
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathon+Funk"} Jonathon Funk
                %em Singular coverings of Toposes
                , Springer Heidelberg 2006. (pp.79ff)
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marta+Bunge"}> Marta Bunge
                ,
                %em Tightly Bounded Completions
                , TAC
                %strong 28
                no.8 (2013) pp.213-240. (
                %a{:href => "http://tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/28/8/28-8abs.html"}> abstract
                )
            %li#BF99
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marta+Bunge"}> Marta Bunge
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathon+Funk"} Jonathon Funk
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On a bicomma object condition for KZ-doctrines
                %strong 143
                (1999) 69-105 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0022-4049(98)00108-X"}> doi:10.1016/S0022-4049(98)00108-X
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                A. J. Power, G. L. Cattani, G. Winskel,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A representation result for free cocompletions
                %a{:href => "        http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/S0022-4049(99)00063-8"} doi
          %p Their distributive laws come into focus in
          %ul#WalkerDL
            %li#MarmolejoDL
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Francisco+Marmolejo"}> Francisco Marmolejo
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Distributive laws for pseudomonads
                %strong 5
                5 (1999) 81-147 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/1999/n5/5-05abs.html"}> tac
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#MW12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Francisco+Marmolejo"}> Francisco Marmolejo
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+J.+Wood"} Richard J. Wood
                %em Kan extensions and lax idempotent pseudomonads
                , TAC
                %strong 26
                no.1 (2012) pp.1-19. (
                %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/26/1/26-01abs.html"}> abstract
                )
            %li
              %p
                Charles Walker,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Distributive Laws via Admissibility
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.09575"} arXiv
          %p
            The relation to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+structures"} Yoneda structures
          %ul#WalkerYS
            %li
              Charles Walker,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Yoneda Structures and KZ Doctrines
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1703.08693"} arxiv
          %p The logical-syntactical side:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jiri+Adamek"}> Jiri Adamek
              , Lurdes Sousa,
              = succeed "," do
                %em KZ-monadic categories and their logic
              %a{:href => "http://tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/32/10/32-10abs.html"} tac
          %p
            Discussion of the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor+theorem"} adjoint functor theorem
          %ul
            %li#ALL23
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nathanael+Arkor"}> Nathanael Arkor
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ivan+Di+Liberti"} Ivan Di Liberti
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fosco+Loregian"} Fosco Loregian
              = succeed "," do
                %em Adjoint functor theorems for lax-idempotent pseudomonads
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.10389"} arXiv:2306.10389
          %p
            On connections to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+multicategories"} generalized multicategories
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+multicategory"} representability
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Claudio+Hermida"}> Claudio Hermida
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em From coherent structures to universal properties
